{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the God of my father Yitzchak.</b> Yet further on he says, ״וּפַחַד יִצְחָק״? And furthermore, what is the reason that he went back and mentioned the special Name? It should have written 'He who said to me, Return to your land,' etc. Rather, thus Yaakov said before the Holy One, blessed be He: Two promises You promised me — one when I left my father's house, from Be'er Sheva, when You said to me ״אֲנִי ה' אֱלֹהֵי אַבְרָהָם אָבִיךָ וֵאלֹהֵי יִצְחָק״, and there You said to me ״וְשַׁמַרְתִּיךָ בְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר תֵּלֵךְ״, and in Bet Lavan's house You said to me (Genesis 31) ״שׁוּב אֶל אֶרֶץ אֲבוֹתֶיךָ וּלְמוֹלַדְתֶּךָ וְאֶהְיֶה עִמָּךְ״ — and there You revealed Yourself to me by the special Name alone, as it says ״וַיֹּאמֶר ה' אֶל יַעֲקֹב שׁוּב אֶל אֶרֶץ אֲבוֹתֶיךָ״ etc. By these two promises I come before You."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:45.337629222Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}